 "thumbnail": "your hand is already",
 "script": "Your friend knocks his coffee off the table, and your hand is already under it before it even starts to fall. Because today, your reaction time is ten times faster. A normal person needs about a quarter of a second to react. You need two and a half hundredths. Sounds amazing, right? Except only your brain got faster. Your body didn't. So when your best friend Leo pitches to you, the ball floats in like a balloon... and you still swing too late. Then comes the school race final. You're crouched at the start, holding yourself back, because if you react in under a tenth of a second, they'll say you guessed and disqualify you. And that's when you see your little brother Sam slipping off the railing. Your brain sees it instantly. Your legs are as slow as ever. The gold medal... or Sam. You run. You catch him. You finish dead last. And Sam just grins at you... right before he knocks his cup off the table.",
